skills/reel-sound-pass/scripts/auphonic.py
  Copied from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/auphonic.py. Changes: it cleans the voice
  track only and no longer puts the sound back on the video; the key comes from the environment or a key file and
  goes only into a request header (urllib instead of curl); plan and run steps with a yes gate and a paid-jobs
  ledger; gaps from the alignment are filled with room tone. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-sound-pass/scripts/_sync.py
  Copied from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/_sync.py. Change: ffmpeg comes from the
  editor install instead of the PATH. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-sound-pass/scripts/mix.py
  Copied from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/mix.py. Changes: rewritten into the sound
  pass's one entry point (quiet gate, stems, free or Auphonic voice clean-up, ratio-keeping sum, master, sound onto
  the picture last, delivery and cue checks); the looped-music path was removed; the free voice filter is kept.
  License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-sound-pass/scripts/_media.py
  Copied from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/_media.py. Changes: ffprobe and ffmpeg come
  from the editor install; it reads the video stream's own length; audio read/write, loudness and workspace helpers
  added; the frame-comparison helpers removed. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-first-cuts/scripts/silence_budget.py
  The fallback silence threshold (22 dB under the 90th percentile of 50 ms windows, never below -55 dB) is
  ported from Shorts Studio, gate/check.py (Claude Video Studio contributors), rewritten in standard-library
  Python. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-first-cuts/scripts/sync.py
  Copied from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/sync.py. Changes: shared helpers and
  ffmpeg/ffprobe come from the editor install; UTF-8 output and plain failures; the low-match stop exits 2.
  License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-first-cuts/scripts/follow_cut.py
  Copied from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/follow_cut.py. Changes: reads cuts.json
  frames, fps and speed; refuses mixed takes; ffmpeg comes from the editor install; frame count asserted;
  UTF-8 output and plain failures. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-first-cuts/scripts/fix_words.py
  Ported from Shorts Studio, scripts/fix_words.py (Claude Video Studio contributors). Changes: it reads S3's
  edit map or a tx.json (`word` or `text`); fixes come from <paths.editor>/word-fixes.json or --map instead of
  --fix; matching is case-insensitive; phrase fixes replace only the last word of a matching sequence; --at
  takes the list index; an edit map's word_list_hash is recomputed and validated; one <name>.prev is kept;
  --cta-check added. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-first-cuts/scripts/repeat_check.py
  Ported from Shorts Studio, scripts/repeat_check.py (Claude Video Studio contributors). The repeat, cut-off,
  restart and retake finder is kept as it was. Changes: it also reads S3's edit map; deep mode uses the
  editor's own transcriber from state.json through transcribe_words.py's route() instead of npx hyperframes,
  and loads the model once per run; ffmpeg comes from the editor's install; windows are sliced with the wave
  module; argparse and UTF-8 output; the temp folder is removed. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-first-cuts/scripts/cut_qa.py
  Rebuilt from Shorts Studio, scripts/qa.py, its "cuts remove only silence" and "no murmur between words"
  checks (Claude Video Studio contributors). Changes: it runs on the gap plan instead of a rendered final
  (cuts.json frames at their own fps, the EDL, probe.py's source envelope and S3's edit map); only silence
  trims inside one EDL cut are checked; murmurs are searched in the kept audio; standalone script with
  --json and an exit code. License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-canvas-build/scripts/placer.py
  Adapted from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), scripts/edit_build.py, hits() and the caption
  spots only. Changes: corner rectangles, master-pixel head mapping, sampled moves, Instagram-safe candidates,
  timed fallback notes and still-graphic overlap notes; the source's graphics zoning is not used.
  License: MIT, full text below.

skills/reel-captions/scripts/captions.py (its auto_chunks part)
  Adapted from shorts-studio (Claude Video Studio contributors), engine/short/gen.py, auto_chunks. Changes:
  output-frame layout boundaries and inclusive word positions. License: MIT, full text below.

